# TDD Skill Activation Rule

When user intent indicates test-first implementation, use the `tdd` skill from `.cursor/skills/tdd/SKILL.md` before coding.

## Trigger signals

Apply this rule when the user:

- explicitly asks for TDD, test-first development, or red-green-refactor
- asks to add/fix a feature with behavior-first tests
- requests higher confidence for bugfixes through automated tests
- asks to implement behavior incrementally with one test at a time

## Expected behavior

- Follow vertical slices: one behavior test -> minimal implementation -> repeat.
- Keep tests focused on public interfaces and observable outcomes.
- Avoid implementation-detail assertions and unnecessary internal mocking.
- Refactor only after GREEN and keep tests passing after each refactor step.

## Non-goals

- Do not force TDD when the task is documentation-only or purely exploratory.
- Do not weaken baseline tests to fit injected-fault behavior.
